' CMDSHELL.UXB -- the 6502DOS shell, a small BASIC (PLAN section 8). Reads a line at the prompt
' and runs its statement: name = expression, PRINT, INPUT, CLS, LOCATE, BEEP, WAIT, PAUSE,
' VERSION, SETSYS, BIND, END, the file statements FILES, LIST, COPY, DELETE, RENAME, MKDIR,
' RMDIR, CHDIR or CD, RUN, IF and ENDIF, and
' in a script ONERROR, GOTO, GOSUB, RETURN, REPEAT and ENDREP. NAME: is a label. Any other name
' runs its BIND alias, or else the program of that name. TO file after a statement sends its
' output to the file; APPEND file adds it to the end of the file; FROM file takes its input from
' the file. A | B runs A with its output into a pipe file, then B with its input from it.
' The code is CMDSHELL.UXI, which src/bank3/ROMSHELL.UXB includes too.
#INCLUDE "DOS.UXI"
#INCLUDE "HEAP.UXI"
#INCLUDE "CMDSHELL.UXI"
